        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "A student wants a scheduling app to read free-and-busy information from a university calendar. The app should not receive the student's password, and it should not gain unlimited access. OAuth solves this delegation problem. The student is the resource owner. The scheduling app is the client. The university identity service acts as authorization server, and the calendar API is the resource server. Keeping these roles separate is the foundation for reasoning about who authenticates, who grants access, who receives tokens, and who stores protected data."
        },
