          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "The client first verifies that returned state matches the stored value. Its backend then sends the authorization code, redirect URI, and original code verifier directly to the token endpoint over a protected channel. The authorization server hashes the verifier and compares it with the earlier challenge. An attacker who intercepted only the code cannot complete this proof. If checks pass, the server returns a scoped access token and, when policy permits, a refresh token. Tokens remain server-side and should be encrypted at rest, narrowly scoped, and handled as credentials."
        },
