        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "The scheduling backend presents the access token to the calendar API, which validates the token and scope before returning only the authorized data. A security review now walks every boundary: exact redirect-URI matching, state validation, PKCE verification, TLS, minimal scopes, token lifetime, secure storage, revocation, and log redaction. OAuth does not make an application secure automatically. It supplies a protocol for delegated access; the implementation must preserve the protocol's assumptions. The most useful test is to ask what an attacker gains from a stolen code, browser history, log entry, access token, or refresh token."
