        "input": {
          "instructions": "Clear, measured, and instructor-ready.",
          "text": "Before redirecting the browser, the client creates two independent values. State binds the returning authorization response to the browser session and helps detect request forgery. The PKCE code verifier is a high-entropy secret held temporarily by the client. The client hashes it to form a code challenge that can safely travel in the authorization request. These mechanisms solve different problems. State protects the transaction's browser context; PKCE later proves that the same client instance redeeming the code initiated the request."
        },
